## 5.4. Time and cumulative patent filing process
The patent filing time trend and cumulative filing time chart are shown in Figs. 28 and 29 for each year in the field of supercapacitor MOF electrodes.
In Fig. 28 we can see that the beginning of filing patents was in 2009 and continued until 2018. The first filed patent was CN101604580, in 2009, by the Shanghai Institute of Ceramics, Chinese Academy of Sciences in China and in the field of porous carbon electrode material by method of decomposing of monophyletic compound. This patent was only filed in China and will expire in 2029 (Legal Status: Alive). In general, the upward trend of patent filing in this field started in 2009 with 1 patent this year and then in 2011, 2 patents were filed. Then, the strong uptrend has begun from 2013, which continues until 2018. Patent filing in this area was not reported in 2010 and 2012, and after 2013 the filing was in a positive trend and the growth illustrates this well. The substantial upward trend in patent filing began in 2014–2015 with 7–8 patents and subsequently intensified until 2018 with 38 patents. The growing trend to 2018 indicates that the technology has begun to grow over the past 10 years and the trend is still ongoing. It is also worth noting that the data for mid-2018 to 2020 are considered as uncertainty data because of the time it takes for the patenting process to be completed and then published and also, there are some restrictions on publishing by the owners themselves. For this reason, patent filing applications per year may be published up to 24 months after the first patent application is filed.
Fig. 29 shows the cumulative diagram of the patenting process for MOF electrodes in supercapacitors and the number of patents filed per year. This chart shows the growth period of the technology. The cumulative patent filing process confirms the annual patent process in this field. An overall growth in three distinct periods of time is observed. The increasing slope from 2013 onwards shows the patent filing increase per year is faster than the year before. Growth was slow in 2009–2012, but steadily increased. The fastest years of technical knowledge growth can be found in 2016–2019. Therefore, considering the three growth periods for technical knowledge in this field, the fastest years of technical knowledge in this field can be found in 2016 to 2019 in which about $92\%$ of all patents were filed in this field of technical knowledge.
## 5.5. Legal status of patents
The legal status of the 113 filed patents in this field is shown in Fig. 30. As shown in Fig. 30, it can be seen that $27\%$ of all filed patents in this field (30 patents) were granted by at least one organization, indicating that the filed patents in this field are high ranked in terms of technical knowledge and considered as valid patents. Also, $92\%$ of all filed patents in this field (104 patents) are legally protected in at least one patent organization (Alive patents). This also indicates the fact that this field of technology is very young and new and has recently been the focus of researchers and companies. Only $8\%$ of filed patents are dead due to being lapsed by the applicants or being revoked.
Only 4 patents of the 135 patents were filed by various companies in this field in more than 15 countries listed in Table 2.
## 5.6. Owners of technical knowledge and protected markets by geographical areas
A survey of 113 patent holders in the field of application of MOFs in supercapacitors shows that these patents have been filed by 86 legal owners from 8 different countries. Fig. 31 shows the legal owners of technical knowledge by geographical area for the 113 filed patents in this field.
As illustrated in Fig. 31, it can be said that the technical knowledge owners in China with 104 patents are the top patent holders in this field of technology. Following that, the US comes in second with 6 patents. Companies from 7 other countries each have less than 2 patents in this field.
Fig. 32 shows the protected markets by geographical areas for the 113 patents in this area. As can be seen, the largest number of patents is filed in China (104 patents), followed by the US with 7 patents and 6 patents were filed as PCT (Patent Cooperation Treaty). Therefore, China may be viewed as the largest market for MOF applications in supercapacitors or the place of the most important competitors and technical knowledge holders.
Hence, it may be concluded that China has the most significant role in patenting and absorbing competitors for MOF applications in supercapacitors.
